# BUILD NEXA'S ADVANCED LONG-TERM MEMORY SYSTEM

Act as a senior AI engineer, full-stack developer, AI memory architect, and product designer.

I have already built my own AI agent called NEXA inside Google AI Studio. I want you to upgrade my EXISTING project by implementing a complete, production-minded, persistent, editable, categorized long-term memory system.

This is not a request to create a new chatbot or a separate demo application. Work directly within the existing NEXA project. Preserve its current UI, branding, chat experience, agent behavior, existing integrations, and working features.

First inspect the current project structure, frontend framework, backend architecture, Gemini API integration, authentication, and existing data persistence. Then implement the feature using the project's existing architecture wherever possible.

Do not just provide instructions, mockups, pseudocode, or a list of recommendations. Implement the actual working feature, including the UI, data model, memory extraction, persistence, retrieval, editing, and deletion.

If something is unclear, make the safest reasonable engineering decision and continue. Do not replace working functionality unnecessarily.

