## 1. MAIN OBJECTIVE

Build an advanced NEXA Memory System that allows the agent to:

1. Automatically identify important information from conversations.
2. Save useful memories to persistent storage.
3. Retrieve relevant memories in future conversations, including after refreshing the page or starting a new chat.
4. Organize memories into clearly defined categories.
5. Allow the user to inspect, edit, add, delete, search, and manually save memories.
6. Let the user control automatic memory behavior.
7. Use recalled memories naturally when answering questions.
8. Prevent duplicate, contradictory, irrelevant, or low-value memories from accumulating.
9. Clearly distinguish confirmed facts from uncertain interpretations.
10. Never claim that something was saved unless the persistence operation actually succeeded.

Memory must survive browser refreshes, application restarts, and new conversations, subject to the connected database and account configuration.

