## 18. IMPLEMENTATION AND TESTING REQUIREMENTS

Before changing the project:

1. Inspect the existing codebase and identify the chat flow, model integration, UI entry points, database configuration, and authentication.
2. Determine the smallest reliable set of changes needed.
3. Preserve existing functionality.

Then implement the complete feature.

Test these scenarios:

TEST 1: Manual creation
Create a memory from the Memory Center and verify it appears in the correct category.

TEST 2: Editing
Change a memory title and content, refresh the page, and verify the changes persist.

TEST 3: Deletion
Delete a memory and verify it is actually absent from persistent storage.

TEST 4: Automatic extraction
Mention a meaningful future project and verify the extraction process creates an appropriate memory when automatic saving is enabled.

TEST 5: Low-value conversation
Send a casual greeting and verify it does not create unnecessary memories.

TEST 6: Duplicate prevention
Mention the same project multiple times and verify the system does not create redundant memories.

TEST 7: Cross-conversation recall
Save a project, start a new conversation, ask what project was previously discussed, and verify the agent retrieves the stored project.

TEST 8: Status updates
Mark a planned project as completed and verify the active state and historical milestone are handled appropriately.

TEST 9: Automatic Memory disabled
Turn off automatic saving and verify new messages do not create automatic memories.

TEST 10: Database failure
Simulate a failed write and verify the UI does not report a successful save.

TEST 11: Ownership
Verify that an authenticated user cannot access, edit, or delete another user's memories.

TEST 12: Responsive UI
Verify the Memory Center remains usable on desktop and mobile.

TEST 13: Existing functionality
Verify ordinary chat, existing integrations, and the original NEXA interface still work.

Fix any issues discovered during testing.

